{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1241380-bonkers-chronicle-idea","id":1241380,"title":"Bonkers Chronicle Idea","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-01T10:45:12-07:00","id":1241380,"title":"Bonkers Chronicle Idea","content":"So i had this idea for a game where basically one gestalt group of supernaturals are all in control of a city, while the pcs are a group of outsiders who will try to take this massive group down. I was pondering ideas for how to combine this. I got the idea from reading the preview of Geist: The Sin-Eaters and the WTF The Pack Book. So what i wanted to figure out was how to best design this group.<br /> <br /> My ideas so far have been sort of like a pyramid scheme:<br /> <br /> A pack of Ghost Wolves who got adopted by a Mummy and who serves as their totem((that example is used in the WTF The Pack book)) that merged in with the mummy's cult + a krewe of Sin-Eaters who merged with the Pack ((that example is also in the pack book)). Beyond that I was even thinking about going so far as having a small court of changelings who have made a pact with this veeeery powerful mummy. ((that example is in the CTL 2nd Edition book)) Since courts don't have to make a deal with cosmic forces and concepts anymore. You could include a couple of Beasts as a member of this mystery cult and a few mages who make it their Nameless Order.<br /> <br /> But with other supernaturals i need the help of you out there in the forumlands! Ideas for how to make this group cohesive and such + how to add more supernaturals to the mix.<br /> <br /> Second i wanted help with pondering which gameline i should use to run the pcs: make it a crossover thing or focus on one specific game and if so then which one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T11:02:24-07:00","id":1241391,"title":"","content":"Since there is enough supernatural shenanigans going on, I'd try to keep the total number in the Gestalt down - so one Mummy, one Beast, a few Werewolves, Changelings, or Vampires. Mages, Demons, and Sin-Eaters could be either singular or in a small number. Prometheans, rare as they are would be either singular or the odd one out. Even if every splat had a single full-template representative, you are looking at 9 members.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-01-2018, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T11:36:03-07:00","id":1241408,"title":"","content":"Do you have any themes or specific plot elements in mind for the group? That might lend some direction regarding suggestions.<br /> <br /> Are they established in the local halls of power? Shadowy masters? Organized Crime? A research group? A Corporation? A Secret Society?<br /> <br /> How old is their alliance? Did they form and take power recently? Long Ago? Were they each separate, but only recently joined forces?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T13:05:19-07:00","id":1241462,"title":"","content":"As for the Organization of the cult, you should consider the structure in detail: Is it one big monolithic thing with the Mummy at the top, or maybe more like a web, with subdivisions?<br /> You could make this easier on the PCs if you go with the idea that the Pack, Krewe, Court, Cults etc don't really know about each other.<br /> A stronger Force would be of course a sort of &quot;Hand&quot; - while everyone is aware of the others, each splat has its place and job within the grand scheme of things (Vampires and Darklings take the Nightshift, Pack is Reconnaisance and Tracking, Mummy and Changelings are Dealmaking and Acquisition etc. etc.). Helps prevent infighting. Especially with Splat combinations (Ogres, Anakim and Rahu to take down a target, Daeva and Fairest for soft social stuff, Ugallu and Ventrue for Hard social stuff)<br /> <br /> You could include vampires by virtue of them looking out for No1, and being part of this powerful group is better than oppose it. Even easier would be a Defiant, since the Ordo is rather interested in studying the Occult, and a Mummy is pretty much their Target Existence in many regards.<br /> You could include a Demon quite easily, because a powerful being like a mummy, with a setup like this cult, is perfect to change infrastructure - even long-term. Their best shot at Hell? As plot hooks, they might be undercover (made a Soul Pact with a Cultist at some point and came claiming and liked what they found a lot). Or the Mummy's right hand man - and Starscream in the making.<br /> Don't include Prometheans, other than as PC, imo. Even Centimani I don't see joining a Cult like this just like that.<br /> Beasts don't need much of a reason for joining, but this cult would be an amazing opportunity for Family Ties and Nightmares.<br /> <br /> In general, I quite like the idea of a Mummy-Totem for a Krewe-Pack, and merging that with a Changeling Motley is awesome.<br /> Getting in Vampires is workable.<br /> Anything else will be at a bit of a stretch imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T14:29:09-07:00","id":1241497,"title":"","content":"i wonder how being a totem would affect the mummy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T18:22:56-07:00","id":1241610,"title":"","content":"As for &quot;Unifying Purpose&quot;, I had the idea of <i>For Science!</i>:<br /> <br /> The Beast, welcoming as they are, seeks to turn their Lair into a welcoming edifice of possibility for their Kin.<br /> The Demon, seeks to build a personal Hell there by making/reassembling Infrastructure in the Chambers (Unchained aren't normally Kin, but the Beast and the Demon's Primary Cover are married, so they are common-law-Kin).<br /> The Vampire is a member of the Ordo Dracul, and sees Wyrm Nest written everywhere.<br /> The Mage is interested in the pure research and Mystery aspects of everything.<br /> The Changeling just wanted somewhere to belong at first, but if these discoveries can give them something to use against the Gentry and/or recover their old life, all the better.<br /> The Mummy finds themselves in this company because their Tomb happens to be once of the Beast's key Chambers (turns out ravaging tomb raiders and Relic thieves leads to Integrity loss). Since the major players are already involved in the area, why not join up? Maybe move their Tomb to one of the Chambers for extra security, if possible. Or see if a Life-web can be set up between the disparate Chamber locations comprising the Lair.<br /> For the Werewolf, they are their Pack. And the new horizons they Hunt are strangely appealing.<br /> The Sin-Eater/Bound is a Thanatologist, and is researching the interplay between Satiety, Integrity loss, and Doppelganger creations.<br /> The Promethean is a Mercurius Scientist on the verge of their own breakthrough.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to inject some Gonzo Humor to it, they could even all be one extended quasi-family, like a villainous Meet the Robinsons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T09:15:31-07:00","id":1241867,"title":"","content":"Oh a question, what gameline should i use for the pcs...Assuming i don't do a mixed chronicle...which one is the most fitting to use for this Chronicle's PCs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T18:16:55-07:00","id":1242171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1241380-bonkers-chronicle-idea?p=1241867#post1241867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh a question, what gameline should i use for the pcs...Assuming i don't do a mixed chronicle...which one is the most fitting to use for this Chronicle's PCs</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunter? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Beast, as the Crossover Splat? Promethean, as the agent-of-chaos, odd-man-out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T19:05:20-07:00","id":1242204,"title":"","content":"Actually, how do you plan on having a promethean as part of it all? He would cause a freaking firestorm wouldn't he being there that long? Unless of course, the promethean is just a regular visitor (actually, do prometheans cause wastelands when in beast lairs, i know they can have great friendship)<br /> <br /> Otherwise, a throng coming in could cause havoc just by being there","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T23:55:05-07:00","id":1242255,"title":"","content":"I<b><i> highly</i></b> advise for having at least one beast PC - character will be innate incentive to sustain all others monsters in it's relations to get opportunity for as many Family Ties and Nightmares, from relationships with other supernaturals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T01:35:01-07:00","id":1242263,"title":"","content":"A Hovel would help mitigate the whole Firestorm busines, but not the problems of Disquiet: Basu-Im is no fun.<br /> I would not include a Promethean as an NPC, but they could work great as PCs (Ferrum, Stannum and Argentum wouldn't even need any additional incentive as their wants to interact and/or challenge/study supernaturals are practically build in, Phosphorus and Cobalus could work rather well, too. Cuprum and Aurum could work at a stretch.)<br /> Beasts could work fine, but a whole brood I wouldnt use.<br /> Vampire might work but they'd be at a severe disadvantage.<br /> Werewolf would work very well, especially if you use Pure for the Mummy's cult.<br /> You could use Mage, Demon or Mummy, might even make that work, but that would render many of the Mummy's subordinates quickly obsolete unless xp-buffed up.<br /> Geist could work well, depending on the cult's actions regarding ghosts.<br /> <br /> The cool thing is that no matter what splats your players use, due to your diverse Cult, there will be things right up their ally, things that will challenge them, and things outide their comfort zone.<br /> So these would work well imo:<br /> A Promethean Throng.<br /> A Pack.<br /> A Krewe<br /> A Pack/Krewe.<br /> + 1-2 Beasts<br /> (I personally would avoid a Cabal or Ring)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T07:23:40-07:00","id":1242345,"title":"","content":"Cool ideas so far <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I just needed some help with pondering the mechanical implications of a Arisen totem as it wasn't discussed in the pack book","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}